heinha@oslonett.no (Hein Haraldsen) writes:

>I was wondering how some of these monsters really look like. Is there a 
>file somewhere which describes them thoroughly? I am particularlily 
>looking for descriptions for rust monsters, mimics, cockatrices, 
>rothes, leocrottas, mumaks, wumpuses, and mind flayers.

I recall finding the Leocrotta in a 12th century bestiary.  Its salient
features are a long, snake-like neck and a sharp ridge instead of teeth.
Wumpuses are definitely modern: they were invented for the computer game
"Wumpus."  All you knew about them was that they were extremely large
(which explains why the super-bats never picked them up), they had suckers
on their feet (which explains how they could stay in the bottomless pit
rooms), and they lived in caves laid out like regular dodecahedra.

